%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: ec4ba6a512adabf4b8a74985cb2f4d14, type: 3}
  m_Name: DioniseIntroDialogue
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ScriptedDialogue
  nodes:
  - type: 0
    npcLine: New to this post. Good. I prefer checkpoints where the officer is still
      paying attention. Complacency tends to set in around the third week.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 0
    npcLine: "Dionise Chkonia. Professor at the university \u2014 philosophy and
      epistemology, though I've been cross-listing into ethics since the situation
      escalated. The administration finds it useful."
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: "I've been through this gate regularly for two years. Today I'm coming
      from the archives \u2014 there are texts I want moved offsite before the dust
      gets worse. Some things are worth the effort to preserve."
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: What kind of texts?
      npcResponse: Primary sources. First editions that exist nowhere else. History
        has a way of surviving in single copies, and I am not prepared to let the
        next one disappear on a shelf no one is maintaining.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    - playerChoiceText: Is the dust getting worse?
      npcResponse: Yes. I don't believe the official picture is complete. It rarely
        is in situations like this. I stopped waiting for full disclosure some time
        ago and began making my own assessments.
      animationTrigger: TalkLookDown
  - type: 0
    npcLine: My students are anxious. Understandably. When everything outside destabilizes,
      people look for structure wherever they can find it. I keep my lectures on
      schedule. It isn't much, but routine is its own form of reassurance.
    animationTrigger: TalkIdle
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
  - type: 1
    npcLine: "I have a wife and two children at home. We're managing. The university
      has been reasonable about supplies \u2014 water filters, medical kits. We're
      not comfortable, but we're not desperate."
    animationTrigger: TalkLookAway
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices:
    - playerChoiceText: How are your children holding up?
      npcResponse: "Better than adults, in some ways. Children adapt. What frightens
        them most isn't the situation itself \u2014 it's watching us pretend we're
        not frightened. So I stopped pretending. It helped."
      animationTrigger: TalkLookDown
    - playerChoiceText: You seem very calm about all of this.
      npcResponse: Stoicism. It is the only rational response to circumstances you
        cannot control. Panic distributes your energy where it does the least good.
        I find it useful to remember that every morning.
      animationTrigger: TalkIdle
  - type: 0
    npcLine: My papers are here. I check them every two weeks precisely to avoid
      holding up checkpoints. The permit runs through June. You should find everything
      straightforward.
    animationTrigger: TalkPoint
    cameraTrigger: 
    wobbleText: 0
    choices: []
